name: the gauntlet
brief: multi-command chains, composed from everything the levels taught -- text triage, then the tradecraft you carry a stick like this to do: name a blob by its magic, carve the secret out of it, count who was refused, find the line where a machine died. thirty seconds each, one life, no hints, no reference. every chain is graded on what your pipe really prints, so any correct pipeline passes. how far can you get?
---
q: %count% the distinct lines of @txt@, with `sort`
a: sort -u @txt@ | wc -l
lvl: 05
ref: sort
---
q: %show% only the lines of @txt@ that appear more than once, with `uniq`
a: sort @txt@ | uniq -d
lvl: 05
ref: uniq
---
q: %count% the @sev@ lines of @log@ with `grep`, a pipe not a flag
a: grep @sev@ @log@ | wc -l
lvl: 06
ref: grep
---
q: %count% the `refused` connections in @log@, with `grep` and a pipe
a: grep refused @log@ | wc -l
lvl: 06
ref: grep
---
q: %show% the last `FATAL` line in @log@, with `grep`
a: grep FATAL @log@ | tail -1
lvl: 06
ref: grep
---
q: %count% the .txt files with `find`, any depth under here
a: find . -name '*.txt' | wc -l
lvl: 07
ref: find
---
q: %show% the status column of @csv@ with `cut`, no header, sorted
a: tail -n +2 @csv@ | cut -d, -f3 | sort
lvl: 08
ref: cut
---
q: %show% @cfg@'s settings with `sed`, key=value, no comments or blanks
a: grep -v '^#' @cfg@ | sed -n 's/ = /=/p'
lvl: 09
ref: sed
---
q: add up the count column of @csv@ with `awk`, skip the header
a: tail -n +2 @csv@ | awk -F, '{s += $4} END {print s}'
lvl: 10
ref: awk
---
q: %list% every severity in @log@ with `awk`, once each
a: awk '{print $3}' @log@ | sort -u
lvl: 10
ref: awk
---
q: %show% the times of the @sev@ lines in @log@ with `awk`, sorted
a: grep @sev@ @log@ | awk '{print $2}' | sort
lvl: 10
ref: awk
---
q: %get% the `refused` address in @log@ with `awk`, listed once
a: grep refused @log@ | awk '{print $NF}' | sort -u
lvl: 10
ref: awk
---
q: %count% the lines across every .log file with `xargs`, one total
a: find . -name '*.log' | xargs wc -l | tail -1
lvl: 19
ref: xargs
---
q: %show% @txt@'s hash with `sha256sum`, nothing after it
a: sha256sum @txt@ | cut -d' ' -f1
lvl: 21
ref: sha256sum
---
q: {name @bin@ by its first eight bytes in hex, one line|read @bin@'s first eight bytes as hex, one line|dump @bin@'s first eight bytes as hex, one line}, with `od`
a: od -A n -t x1 -N 8 @bin@ | head -1
lvl: 22
ref: od
---
q: {pull the readable `unlock` string buried in @bin@|carve the `unlock` string out of @bin@|dig out @bin@'s string that mentions unlocking}, with `strings`
a: strings @bin@ | grep unlock
lvl: 22
ref: strings
---
q: %count% the `processor` lines in `/proc/cpuinfo` with `grep`, a pipe not a flag
a: grep processor /proc/cpuinfo | wc -l
lvl: 24
ref: grep
---
q: %count% the `inet` addresses on this machine, with `ip`
a: ip addr | grep -c inet
lvl: 25
ref: ip
---
q: %show% just the `roothash` value from `/proc/cmdline`, with `tr`
a: tr ' ' '\n' < /proc/cmdline | grep roothash | cut -d= -f2
lvl: 30
ref: tr
